From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nitin Gote <nitin.r.gote@intel.com>
Date: Mon, 15 Sep 2026 10:00:00 +0530
Subject: Gate xe_i2c on i2c-designware Xe backport availability

The Xe I2C/AMC support requires the in-kernel i2c-designware driver to
carry the Intel Xe enablement (generic polling mode, poll-by-default when
there is no IRQ resource, and the parent-regmap "intel,xe-i2c" quirk).
On a kernel without those changes, registering the i2c_designware
platform device makes the built-in driver fail probe with
"IRQ index 0 not found" / "invalid resource" (KERN_ERR).

autoconf (AC_XE_I2C_SUPPORTED) defines BPM_XE_I2C_NOT_SUPPORTED when the
target kernel does not export the dummy symbol i2c_designware_xe_backport
(checked via Module.symvers). In that case, make xe_i2c_probe() a no-op so
no platform device is registered. All other xe_i2c entry points already
early-return when xe->i2c is NULL, so this single guard is sufficient.

Signed-off-by: Nitin Gote <nitin.r.gote@intel.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_i2c.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_i2c.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_i2c.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_i2c.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_i2c.c
@@ -354,6 +354,12 @@ int xe_i2c_probe(struct xe_device *xe)
 	struct xe_i2c *i2c;
 	int ret;
 
+#ifdef BPM_XE_I2C_NOT_SUPPORTED
+	drm_info(&xe->drm,
+		 "Kernel i2c-designware lacks Intel Xe support; skipping Xe I2C/AMC\n");
+	return 0;
+#endif
+
 	if (!xe->info.has_i2c)
 		return 0;
 
